		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=26623#p26623"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Le plus simple est de tester, non ?</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>postgres=# create table t1(c1 integer, c2 text);
CREATE TABLE
postgres=# insert into t1 values (1, &#039;un&#039;);
INSERT 0 1
postgres=# create materialized view mv1 as select * from t1;
SELECT 1
postgres=# select * from mv1;
 c1 | c2 
----+----
  1 | un
(1 row)

postgres=# insert into mv1 values (2, &#039;deux&#039;);
ERROR:  cannot change materialized view &quot;mv1&quot;
postgres=# update mv1 set c2=&#039;deux&#039; where c1=1;
ERROR:  cannot change materialized view &quot;mv1&quot;
postgres=# delete from mv1 where c1=1;
ERROR:  cannot change materialized view &quot;mv1&quot;</code></pre></div><p>Donc non, ce n&#039;est pas possible <img src="http://forums.postgresql.fr/img/smilies/smile.png" width="15" height="15" alt="smile" /></p>]]></content>
